  "narration": {
    "path": "voice/take_01.wav",
    "script": "If your potatoes keep welding to the pan, the mistake started right here in the sink. Peeling and washing whole potatoes removes dirt, but the real trouble happens the moment you slice them. Your knife shears open thousands of cells, flooding the cut surfaces with sticky free starch. Rinsing those cut wedges under running water washes that cloudy starch away, so they brown cleanly instead of sticking.",
    "delivery": "Calm, curious, connected explanation to a friend in the kitchen",
